  "ports": [
    "FJ_KeyboardButtons uses TextInputBG/TextInputBGBorder and LayoutButton_Outline, not scaled main-menu bevels. Existing text images are reused.",
    "LaunchMoreOptionsMenuExtended centers tab labels and keeps each tab focus independent. Unsupported online/trust/PVP controls collapse before the retained game-option rows.",
    "One original Superflat World checkbox owns flat mode. Java terrain variants use a separate non-flat cycle; customizer replaces that cycle while flat mode is active.",
    "LegacyFlatWorldScreen supplies Layers/Biomes/Properties, top-to-bottom visual order over bottom-to-top storage, add/edit/delete/move, preset application and apply-on-close.",
    "FlatWorldLayerSelector supplies the 10-column block grid, native item variants, height slider and OK application. Existing original panels, slots and fonts are reused."
  ],
  "adaptations": [
    "The supplied LCE source includes only a Superflat toggle, without a layer customizer. No missing C++ implementation or assets are claimed; the editor is a Legacy4J Java API port.",
    "Hardcore is a requested Java-only fifth difficulty choice. It uses native 1.11 hardcore and fixes Hard difficulty; permanent Survival/no-privilege and Hardcore provenance locks are user-requested rules.",
    "Java 1.11 has height 256 and native flat-generator feature names. Unsupported 1.20 structures/biomes are omitted. One layer is retained to avoid empty-preset fallback.",
    "World types, layer selectors and live control callbacks retain native Minecraft generation and persistence. No image artwork is invented."
  ]
